      "peak_block": "Brazilian ponta (18:00-21:00, Mon-Fri)",
      "peak_note": "Brazil has settled a genuinely hourly PLD since January 2021, so it has no traded peak block. The ponta window is a distribution-tariff construct whose exact hours each distributor sets locally; 18:00-21:00 is the common case and is used here only to make Brazil comparable with other markets. Do not read it as a wholesale product.",
      "notes": "A continent-scale hydro-dominated system operated as a single optimised cascade, where price is a model output rather than an auction clearing. Reservoir storage substitutes for the fuel-cost stack that sets price elsewhere, so scarcity shows up as a stored-energy problem first.",
